## Who is a preventive stay ideal for?

- **40+** — the age when it pays to start monitoring cardiovascular risks
- **Sedentary occupations** — programmers, managers, drivers
- **Family history** — diabetes, hypertension, cancer in the family
- **Post-Covid** — persistent fatigue, shortness of breath, reduced fitness
- **Stress and burnout** — burnout prevention is cheaper than treatment

## What the numbers say

Studies by the Czech Inspectorate of Spas and Springs show that patients who complete a preventive spa stay at least once a year have:

- a **34 % lower** incidence of cardiovascular events
- a **28 % lower** consumption of pain medication
- a **41 % better** subjective assessment of quality of life

## Marienbad and prevention: what makes it unique

Marienbad has more than 40 mineral springs of varying composition — from iron-rich to alkaline. This enables an **individualised drinking cure** tailored to your specific health profile.

The natural CO₂ gas that rises from the ground here is used in [carbon dioxide baths and dry gas baths](/en/co2-therapy). These demonstrably dilate blood vessels, improve circulation and lower blood pressure — ideal prevention of cardiovascular disease.

And [climatotherapy](/en/climatotherapy) — medically prescribed forest walks with a defined gradient — is prevention that requires no equipment whatsoever. Just forest, air and movement.

## When to visit?

The best time for a preventive stay is **whenever you feel well**. That is precisely when prevention makes the most sense. The recommended length of stay is 5–7 days for the basic programme, 14 days for a comprehensive preventive cure.

More about [planning your stay](/en/practical-information) and [accommodation](/en/accommodation) in Marienbad.
